# Copyright headers

Every Rust source file (`.rs`) must begin with this copyright line, followed by a blank line, then module docs (`//!`) and/or code:

```rust
// Copyright (C) 2026 Chris Burdess <dog@gnu.org>

//! Module documentation…
```

## Rules

- Place the copyright **before** `//!` crate/module docs and before `use` / `mod` / items.
- Do not omit it on new files, examples, tests, or stubs.
- Do not invent a longer LGPL header unless the user asks; this one-line form is the project standard.
- If editing a file that lacks the header, add it as part of the change.
